# Milestone: M3
# Covers: variables declared in '&' and ',' branches are unscoped into the
#         parent environment (not local to the branch block).
# defer-to: M5 (requires '&' and ',' separator runtime and unscoping semantics)
#
# Reason:
#   The fixture exercises that 'var a & var b' and 'var a,' declared inside a
#   compound separator expression escape their branch and are visible in the
#   parent block.  This unscoping semantic requires the '&' and ',' separator
#   runtime in the chk driver (M5).  The semantics themselves are part of the
#   §7.1 shared-frame design (design-risks-7, M5+).
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M5 with unscoping semantics):
# # { var a & var b; a; b; void };
# # { var a, a; void };
